        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. US finds huge tunnel on the Mexican border used to smuggle drugs Americas Issued on: 03/06/2026 - 15:11 Modified: 03/06/2026 - 15:11 Mexican authorities have discovered an illegal tunnel that is 600 metres long on the US border with Mexico. It links Tijuana with the city of San Diego. Its purpose? Possibly the illegal smuggling of drugs. The discovery was the result of a six-month long investigation. Wembanyama chases NBA dream ahead of Spurs-Nicks final 03/06/2026 Americas As California votes in the primary elections, who are the candidates? 03/06/2026 Americas Californian elections test for divided Democrats on pivotal primary election day 03/06/2026 Americas Pro-Trump candidate lead in Colombia 'part of Donroe doctrine' asserting itself in region 01/06/2026 Americas Centenary of Marilyn Monroe: 'Just as relevant now as she was then' 01/06/2026 Culture How to handle armed groups? Colombians vote in presidential election 31/05/2026 Americas \"Fujimori never again!\" Protesters fill streets of Lima ahead of Peru presidential elections 31/05/2026 Americas US says 'more than capable' of resuming war, as peace deal remains elusive 30/05/2026 Americas How to to end edemic violence in Colombia? Presidential elections to take place on Sunday 30/05/2026 Americas"
